.TH "CSSROTATE.CSSROTATE" "3JS" "October 13, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSRotate.CSSRotate \- CSSRotate: CSSRotate() constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSRotate()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates a new
\f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] object representing the \f[CR]rotate()\f[R] value
of the individual \f[CR]transform\f[R] property in CSS.
.PP
This can be specified as either a 2D rotation by a particular angle, or
as a 3D rotation by an angle around a particular axis.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new CSSRotate(angle)
new CSSRotate(x, y, z, angle)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]angle\f[R]
A value for the angle of rotation of the \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] object to
be constructed.
This must be a \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]x\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A number or \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] value indicating the
x\-coordinate of the rotation axis vector of the \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R]
object to be constructed.
Only used, and required, when constructing a 3D rotation; the
2\-argument form implies a rotation axis of \f[CR](0, 0, 1)\f[R] (the
z\-axis).
.TP
\f[B]y\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A number or \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] value indicating the
y\-coordinate of the rotation axis vector of the \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R]
object to be constructed.
Only used, and required, when constructing a 3D rotation.
.TP
\f[B]z\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A number or \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] value indicating the
z\-coordinate of the rotation axis vector of the \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R]
object to be constructed.
Only used, and required, when constructing a 3D rotation.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Raised if the value of the \f[CR]angle\f[R] property is not an
\f[CR]<angle>\f[R] value or \f[CR]CSSRotate.x\f[R],
\f[CR]CSSRotate.y\f[R], \f[CR]CSSRotate.z\f[R] are not
\f[CR]<number>\f[R] values.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Constructing a 2D rotation
The 2\-argument form takes only an angle, and implies a rotation around
the z\-axis (equivalent to \f[CR]rotate3d(0, 0, 1, angle)\f[R]):
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] rotate2D = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSRotate(CSS.deg(45));

console.log(rotate2D.is2D); \f[I]// true\f[R]
console.log(rotate2D.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqrotate(45deg)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.SS Constructing a 3D rotation
The 4\-argument form takes the rotation axis coordinates followed by the
angle:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] rotate3D = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSRotate(1, 1, 0, CSS.deg(45));

console.log(rotate3D.is2D); \f[I]// false\f[R]
console.log(rotate3D.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqrotate3d(1, 1, 0,45deg)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.SS Handling an invalid angle
.IP
.EX
\f[B]try\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] rotate = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSRotate(CSS.px(45));
} \f[B]catch\f[R] (e) {
  console.log(e); \f[I]// TypeError: px is not an angle\f[R]
}
.EE
